# Full bug log + pack rails (Lexora / law-firm-1, 2026-10-16)

Every item below bit production editor. New ZIP packs must prevent them at source; editor rails are backup only.

## A) Dual breadcrumb on About (and other inners)

**Symptom:** White `Home / About Us` + dark hero `Home → About Us` (two crumbs).

**Cause:** Classic `ensureMissingPageBreadcrumbs` injects `Breadcrumb-1` while pack already has `AboutBreadcrumb` / `LexoraAboutBreadcrumb1`.

**Pack / editor rules:**

- Theme stack lists theme crumb (`AboutBreadcrumb`, `TeamBreadcrumb`, …) — never rely on generic Breadcrumb alone if design has a hero crumb.
- Strip/skip generic `Breadcrumb` / `Breadcrumb-*` when page stack or siblings already have `*Breadcrumb`.
- `pageBodyHasOwnBreadcrumb` / theme-upload branch must treat named crumbs as “has crumb”.

## B) Extra “About Story” (classic AboutPage)

**Symptom:** Generic “We build thoughtful websites…” block on About.

**Cause:** `addAboutPageSection` → `AboutPage-1` because Lexora uses `AboutFirm` etc., not id `AboutPage`.

**Rules:**

- Theme Upload open path: do **not** run `addAboutPageSection` / ServicePage / GalleryPage / ContactPage / EventPage injectors.
- `alignThemeUploadTemplatePages`: drop classic `*Page` / `AboutPage-*` bodies not listed in `pages[].sections`.
- Skip `ensureMissingAboutPageCompanions` for Theme Upload.

## C) Extra “Practical next steps” / CustomPageDetail

**Symptom:** Long filler “Next steps for Our Team…” above theme team hero; toolbar “Our Team details”.

**Cause:** `ensureCustomPageScaffold` / `createCustomPageDetailSection` from label “Our Team” → slug `our-team`, no manager body match.

**Rules:**

- Never scaffold CustomPage on a slug that matches a `theme.json` page (id / label / team↔teams↔our-team).
- Strip `CustomSection` / `CustomPage` / `CustomPageDetail-*` from Theme Upload pages when not in stack.
- `addCustomPageSectionsForLinks`: resolve page from **href `#page-*`**, not only `createPageSlug(label)`.

## D) Ghost page `our-team` vs real `team` / `teams`

**Symptom:** `?page=teams` works; `?page=our-team` auto-appears empty/wrong.

**Cause:** Label “Our Team” → slug `our-team`; `normalizePageSlug` did not alias; `recoverCustomPageLinksFromSections` created `#page-our-team`; PreviewContext wrote URL from label when href miss.

**Rules:**

- Canonical page id = `theme.json` `pages[].id` (e.g. `team`).
- Aliases in `normalizePageSlug` / `editorPageSlugsMatch`: `our-team` ↔ `team` ↔ `teams` (and similar for other labels).
- Theme Upload menu: `createPageSlug(page.id)` → `#page-team`; do **not** `canonicalizeTeamPageLink` → `#page-teams` for packs that use `team`.
- `isTeamPageLink` must match “Our Team” / `our-team` / `#page-team`.
- Preview URL: prefer `#page-*` from menu href over `normalizePageSlug(label)`.
- Reserved slugs for recover-custom: include `team`, `teams`, `our-team`.

## E) Two “Home” in Multi Pages switcher

**Symptom:** Home listed twice.

**Cause:** `theme.json` includes `id: home` in `pages[]` and switcher also prepends Home.

**Rules:**

- `editorPageSwitcherLinks` / `buildTemplateMultiPageMenu`: prepend Home once; filter `id === "home"` from theme page list when building order.
- Do not emit second `#page-home`.

## F) Stacked Topbars / Headers on inner pages (“chrome spam”)

**Symptom:** Dozens of topbars/headers on About.

**Cause:** Theme Upload clones Topbar/Header/Footer onto every page; editor showed all PAGE_SHELL types for the page.

**Rules:**

- Per editor page: show **one** Topbar + **one** Header + page body + **one** Footer (page-scoped chrome for that slug, or home chrome — not every page’s copy).
- `isPageShellVisibleOnEditorPage` / visibility must pick the matching page’s shell only.

## G) Admin / scope / Our Team page open

**Symptom:** Wrong admin page scope; Our Team did not open (`our-team` ≠ `team`).

**Rules:**

- Admin page select / scope uses same slug aliases as editor.
- Compose preview aliases (`lexoraPreview`, compose `PAGE_ALIASES`): `/our-team` → `#page-team`, `/team` → `#page-team`.

## H) Logo — no pencil on Header/Footer

**Symptom:** Hover logo → no edit pencil.

**Cause:** Text/crest logo only; no `data-editor-media*`; field was `image` not `logoImage`; `replaceHintedMediaValue` required existing string `logoImage`.

**Rules:**

- Always media target: `data-editor-media`, `type=image`, `role=logo`, `src`, `overlay=show`.
- Read `logoImage || image`; write both on upload.
- Allow setting `logoImage` when previously undefined; sync `image`.
- Placeholder transparent SVG src OK so hover works before first upload.
- `editorFields`: include `logoImage`, `image`, logo text fields.

## I) Header two CTAs disappeared (Contact Us / Book Consultation)

**Symptom:** Preview Vercel has two pills; editor header had none.

**Cause:** `component.json` stores **strings** `"Contact Us"` / `"Book Consultation"`; code checked `contactButton?.label` (object only).

**Rules:**

- Resolve CTA as string **or** `{ label, url|href }` with fallbacks `/contact`, `/book-consultation`.
- Always render both CTAs (design defaults if missing).
- Style match source (pill + arrow circle); hrefs via `toLestowHref`.
- Do not hide CTAs behind `hidden xl:flex` only — keep `sm:flex` / always-visible consult like source.

## J) Theme Color — accents / icons not updating

**Symptom:** Headings change; icons, READ MORE, process alt cards, badges stay gold/grey/hardcoded.

**Cause:** Hardcoded `#c49250`, `#c09665`, `#b58d56`, `#051024`; accents mapped to `--secondary-bg` while user only changes Primary; sticky `theme-upload-css-vars` inject.

**Rules:**

- Pack rewrite all brand hex:
  - Accent/CTA/icon/gold family → `var(--primary-bg,#c49250)` (and gold variants `#c09665`, `#b58d56`, `#e0b467`, `#a87b3f`)
  - Dark navy/ink/footer/topbar → `var(--hero-bg,#051024)` (also `#0a1828`, `#0b1a36`, `#001736`)
- **Never** bind both accent and navy to the same CSS variable.
- Strip `theme-upload-css-vars` / fixed `:root{--color-primary…}` injects from packed TSX.
- Soft gold washes → `color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary-bg) …%, white)`.

## K) Theme Fonts — headings still look sans

**Symptom:** Playfair selected; footer “PRACTICE AREAS” / UI look Inter.

**Rules:**

- Ship `--font-heading`, `--font-body`, `--font-button` in `theme.json` variables.
- Rely on `[data-site-theme-root] h1–h6 { font-family: var(--font-heading) }` — use real heading tags for section titles where design allows.
- Do not hardcode `font-family: Inter` on headings in packed CSS/TSX.

## L) Theme Color Reset default → wrong palette (Ocean teal)

**Symptom:** Reset made buttons teal `#00cadd` instead of preview gold ([law-firm-1 preview](https://lestow.com/preview/Law%20Firm/theme/law-firm-1)).

**Cause:** `getTemplateVariables` fell through to `templates[0]` (Realestate Ocean) when law-firm vars empty; `applyLawFirmVariableFallbacks(template.id)` used wrong id; DB `variables: {}`.

**Rules:**

- Pack **must** include full `variables` (see §1 below).
- On upload, persist variables to DB (never leave empty).
- `getTemplateVariables(requestedId)`: resolve vars from **found** template only — never borrow `templates[0]` colors.
- Law-firm (and future families): fallback defaults keyed by **requested** `templateId` (`law-firm-*`), matching compose preview.
- Reset default label/action: replace COLOR_FIELDS from that template’s defaults (gold/navy for Lexora), not session baseline / Ocean.

## M) Create-with-AI isolation (do not mix)

- Theme Upload / Redesign / template Create stay separate from `create-ai/*`.
- Do not bolt Create-AI hamburger / fake chrome onto Theme Upload Lexora.

## N) Assets / preview

- All media in pack → Theme Upload S3 rewrite; no bare `/banner/...` in defaultContent for live preview.
- `previewImage` + home preview must load after upload.
- `mapThemeUploadAssetsInData` / family asset helper on every component that uses images.
- **New themes (2026-10-23+):** do not import `lib/restaurantFoodAssets`. Give each theme its own mapper, e.g. `lib/weddingPlannerAssets.ts`, `lib/inkvibeAssets.ts`, and import that from every component in the pack. `restaurantFoodAssets.ts` stays only for themes already shipped on it. Do not add new families into that file.

## O) Admin category / scope

- Upload with correct `categorySlug` (Law Firm ≠ Restaurant).
- Admin template page scope lists pack `pages[]` ids; selecting About/Team uses aliases above.
- Do not force Restaurant* variants on law-firm packs.

